  "query_preview": "(Saturday through Tuesday)...\nHigh clouds will increase again for Friday night and Saturday.\nHigh pressure aloft will begin to weaken on Saturday and onshore\nlower-level flow will return. High temperatures for the coast and\nvalleys will cool 4 to 8 degrees on Saturday with high\ntemperatures for the coast and valleys mostly in the mid 70s to\naround 80. High temperatures will continue to cool through \nTuesday with high temperatures for the coast and valleys on\nTuesday ranging from the mid 60s for the far inland valleys to \naround 70 for coastal areas.\n\nA fast-moving low pressure system moving inland across California\non Sunday will bring a chance of showers for Sunday night and\nMonday. A stormier pattern may develop across the Pacific into \nCalifornia for the rest of next week, but with lower confidence in\nthe timing and track of individual systems. A low pressure system\narriving some time around Tuesday and Wednesday could bring \nstrong winds and heavy precipitation to southwestern California, \nbut with lower confidence in the details. \n\nFor Tuesday morning through Thursday night, the chance for 1 inch\nor more of rainfall from the coast to the mountains ranges from \n75 to 85 percent for Orange and southwestern San Bernardino \nCounties, to around 60 percent across southern San Diego County. \nChances for 3 inches or more of rainfall ranges from 5 to 10 \npercent near the coast to 25 to 35 percent for the mountains.",
